[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    27[0m:[38;5;10m[49m   both infinities, both zeros and subnormals) — rows 12–15.
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    28[0m:[38;5;10m[49m * `errno` is the *only* thing the C branches on, so the trigger for each row
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    29[0m:[38;5;10m[49m   is "an input pair for which glibc's `pow` sets that `errno`". Rows 1–8
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    30[0m:[38;5;10m[49m   enumerate the distinct ways glibc reaches `EDOM` / `ERANGE`; verified
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    31[0m:[38;5;10m[49m   against glibc directly.
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    32[0m:[38;5;10m[49m * Both error paths also emit a message. "Same rejection" is asserted as
