[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    20[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    21[0m:[38;5;10m[49m **Input shapes** — the entire input space is two IEEE-754 binary64 values.
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    22[0m:[38;5;10m[49m The shapes the code (via glibc `pow`) distinguishes are: sign of base;
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    23[0m:[38;5;10m[49m integrality/parity of exponent; the five FP classes (normal, subnormal, zero,
